+## Summary of the change
+
+- `src/flask/cli.py`
+  - Added `_get_rule_domain(rule)` which returns `rule.host` for host-matched rules, else `subdomain.SERVER_NAME` (or just the subdomain / just `SERVER_NAME`).
+  - `routes_command` now renders a **Domain** column (first column) when at least one rule is bound to a domain, and adds `"domain"` to the `--sort` choices.
+  - For apps with no domains the output is byte-for-byte the same as before, so existing `flask routes` tests keep passing.
+- `tests/test_cli.py`
+  - Kept the existing `TestRoutes` tests untouched.
+  - Added `test_no_domain_without_server_name`, `test_domain`, and `test_sort_domain`.
